{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development by reason of its size and design would result in a shop unit with&amp;nbsp;a GIA of ~7sqm with a floor to ceiling height of ~2.4m and poor street presence, the proposal is therefore considered&amp;nbsp;to have inadequate floor space, for the units to operate independently&amp;nbsp;as separate planning/commercial units. As such is contrary to:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Paragraph 126 of the National Planning Policy Framework (&lt;span class=&quot;scayt-misspell-word&quot; data-scayt-word=&quot;NPPF&quot; data-wsc-lang=&quot;en_GB&quot; data-wsc-id=&quot;lxu8kr8aykdppkztf&quot;&gt;NPPF&lt;/span&gt;)&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy SD7 (Town centres:&amp;nbsp;development principles and Development Plan Documents), Policy D4 (Delivery good design) and Policy HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan, &lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy CP3 (High quality built environment) and&amp;nbsp;Policy CP2 (Protection and Promoting our Historic Environment) of the Core Strategy, &lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy BP11 (Urban design) and Policy BP2 (Conservation areas and Listed Buildings) of the Borough Wide Development Policies DPD, &lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Strategic policy SP 2 (Delivering a high quality and resilient built environment)&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy&amp;nbsp;DMD 1 (Securing high-quality design) and Policy DMD 4 (Heritage assets and archaeological remains) of the Draft Local Plan 2037 (Reg 19).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development by reason of the lack of clarity and information provided, given the unclear end use of the units, especially the smaller of the two proposed and&amp;nbsp;no information&amp;nbsp;provided with respect to servicing, waste, recycling storage and collection, or cycle storage provision, is considered to be inappropriate and&amp;nbsp;unacceptable for when assessing this application. Thus, is contrary to:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Paragraph 3.3.18 and Policy T5 (Cycling) and Table 10.2 of the London Plan&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy BR15 (Sustainable waste management) and Policy BP8 (Protecting residential amenities) and&amp;nbsp;Policy BR9 (Parking) from the&amp;nbsp;Borough Development Policies DPD&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Part 3 in Policy DMSI 8 (Demolition, construction and operational waste) and Policy DMT 3 (Cycle parking)&amp;nbsp;of the draft Local Plan 2037&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
